A||N||11||DisfourDan||Getting my First FIERO||||1||
Z||000000||DisfourDan||05-21-2001||11:36 AM||||hey guys, in a few weeks I am getting my first fiero, I found someone that has the 1987 model of it.  he says it is in good condition, no body damage, runs strong, and is selling it for 1700$ or best offer.  Miles are somewhere near 100K.  I am planning to go take a look at it soon.  Anything i should check for?  I am planning to make this fiero look bada$$.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||11:53 AM||||I would have to say it depends on the model. If its a GT, thats a good deal. If its a coupe, it could be depending on how good a shape it really is.<P>Here is a link to a good Fiero pricing guide: <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/Price%20Guide.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/Price%20Guide.htm</A> <P>Good luck, also one tip: there are a ton of Fieros out there for sale, make sure you buy the one you want (i.e. look at coupes, Formulas and GTs before you buy the first one you look at)<BR>Don't rush- there are lots of people who think Fieros are crap and will sell you a nice solid car pretty darn cheap!<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>        <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48495967&Sequence=0&res=high">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||05-21-2001||12:12 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I do agree with Lisa I have not paid more than 650 for any of my 4 Fieros granted all are 2.5 notchbacks and in various conditions but still there are a lot of decent cars out there<P>84 Indy $400<BR>84 SE $600<BR>86 Cpe $650<BR>88 Cpe $400<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||05-21-2001||12:42 PM||||Your all making me feel stupid. I paid 2600 for my coupe last year. Its a 88 base coupe with 45k miles(last year). Did I get riped off?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000004||Raydar||05-21-2001||12:59 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>Your all making me feel stupid. I paid 2600 for my coupe last year. Its a 88 base coupe with 45k miles(last year). Did I get riped off?     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think so. Especially if you're happy with it.<BR>3 years ago, I paid $2000 for my 88 coupe with nearly 120,000 miles. Body and interior were flawless, though.<BR>2 years ago, I paid $3450 for my T-top Formula. Was pretty ratty.<BR>Did I pay too much? Maybe. But it was what I wanted at the time. Was fortunate enough to have the cash handy. <BR>Would I pay that much now? Probably not, but it depends. If I had the cash, and saw something I couldn't live without, I just might. (Of course, I would be exiled to the couch, but that's for another thread.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I <I>am</I> able to make much more informed decisions as a result of being a part of this Forum.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||05-21-2001||01:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>Your all making me feel stupid. I paid 2600 for my coupe last year. Its a 88 base coupe with 45k miles(last year). Did I get riped off?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heck no! 45K miles in great condition is a really good price.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||05-21-2001||01:33 PM||||$1700 sounds like it may be a bit high if its not in good shape.  However, if the frame is in good shape, and the paint/interior are good it may be fine.  Be sure the engine seems sound.  My dads old 87 duke bit the dust at 95K.  Cam gears were bad and it was blowing oil out the tail pipe!  He put a new engine in it and its still going stong for its new owner (my cousin)at 130K!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||05-21-2001||01:44 PM||||The problem with buying cars like the Fiero is you will ALWAYS find a better deal 3 months after you bought your car!<P>The bottom line is if you are happy with it, then it was a good deal.  <P>I paid $3100 for my blue GT last fall with about 90K on it.  Ran really well and it is in very good shape but I had to rebuild the front suspension and a few other deferred maintenance stuff.  I probably could have found a better deal but I like the car and it has been pretty reliable.<P>Enjoy it!!!<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||05-21-2001||01:48 PM||||two expensive things to fix is if its a stick, make sure the clutch works properly, and expecially on V6 make sure all the exhaust is Ok. Rusted manifolds, etc can cost you some bucks to replace. If you dont replace the manifolds yourself, the dealer charges $400 per side give or take. (depends on how many studs break, mine broke 6)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero5||05-21-2001||02:24 PM||||Yeah, Lisa is right. There are a lot of great deals out there. There are also some right here on Pennocks. I just saw a thread either on here or on one of the Fiero lists the other day for an 85GT for $1,100. bucks!<BR>What a deal that is (or was).<P>BTW: Lisa, do you offer photo-op posing like that on other peoples Fieros too?<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
